d welcome catherine um bring us up  to date what what more do we know  in the last few hours police have gone  into the  home of the assailant nafar from the  police station in hambury to the  southwest of paris  we also know that they're carrying out a  search of his previous home which is in  eastern paris  police have also taken into custody for  questioning  three of members of his close entourage  we understand one of those could be a  family  member in the meantime police also say  they have his  mobile phone they're going through that  to see what sort of links he may have  had  uh in the last few hours before this  attack took place  whether they were links to jihadist  organizations or  or anyone that can give them some sort  of clue  as to where this man was coming from  what he was doing  who were his accomplices if indeed there  were any because this is a  a man who was not known to the security  services he wasn't known to the  intelligence services  so they're really just fumbling around  at this moment to try and  put together a picture of what actually  happened in those  minutes before this attack took place  and this is now being treated as a  terror attack so what what difference  does that make in terms of powers of  arrest and the way that the  investigation is handled  it means that the anti-terror  prosecutors can call on the  french domestic intelligence unit it  means that they can  have much more wider scope will be able  to  draw in other witnesses they can hold  people for longer  and of course they have all this other  information to have that they've had  unfortunately from other attacks there's  been a spate  over the last five or six years of  attacks on  very small police stations and homes of  police officers  uh in the western paris area so they'll  be able to get all that information  together  very quickly and try and find out yet  once again  what went wrong that an armed attacker  was able to get  through the front door of a police  station and stabbed to death  a police employee and what sort of place  is rambu where this attack happened  it's a very quiet little suburban town  really it's about 60 kilometers  southwest of paris it has a  fast train service into the french  capital so the sort of people who live  there are generally  families you can have a very small house  with a little small garden  uh the area is also known for having a  beautiful  forest a lovely chateau it's where you  would really go  to get away from the sort of hustle and  bustle of the city and i think  that's why uh the scenes that we're  seeing tonight in rambia are just so  shocking because people are wandering  around the street saying  how could this have happened in this  quiet sleepy little commuter town  uh where everyone has always been known  for being friendly and law-abiding  thank you for that uh catherine  journalist catherine field in paris  thank you
 

